RIGHT COMFORT WEBSITE - SIMPLE GUIDE & INSTRUCTIONS
===================================================

WHAT IS THIS WEBSITE AND HOW DOES IT WORK?
-------------------------------------------
Your website (rightcomfort.ca) is stored on GitHub and delivered to visitors by Cloudflare.

Think of it like this:
1. GitHub is your digital filing cabinet where your website files (like index.html) live.
2. Cloudflare is your automatic publisher that takes your files from GitHub and shows them to anyone visiting rightcomfort.ca.
3. Every time you save a change on GitHub, Cloudflare automatically updates your live website in less than a minute!


WHERE ARE YOUR WEBSITE FILES?
-----------------------------
* index.html : This is your main web page containing all the written text, phone numbers, and section headings.
* style.css  : This controls the look of your website (colors, font sizes, spacing, and button styles).
* images/    : The folder holding pictures, icons, and logo files used on your site.


HOW TO CHANGE TEXT OR PHONE NUMBERS ON YOUR WEBSITE
--------------------------------------------------
Step 1: Open GitHub in your web browser.
        Go to: https://github.com/gulzaryyz/RightComfort-website

Step 2: Click on the file you want to edit.
        (Usually "index.html" to change words, services, or phone numbers).

Step 3: Click the Pencil icon in the top-right corner to start editing.

Step 4: Make your text changes.

Step 5: Save your changes.
        Click the "Commit changes..." button at the top right, type a short note about what you changed (for example: "Updated phone number"), and click "Commit changes".

That is all! Cloudflare will automatically publish your updated site in 15 to 30 seconds.


WHAT TO DO IF YOU DON'T SEE YOUR CHANGES RIGHT AWAY
----------------------------------------------------
If you saved your changes on GitHub, but rightcomfort.ca still shows the old version:

1. Refresh your browser memory (Cache):
   On Linux / Windows (Chrome): Press Ctrl + Shift + R
   On Mac: Press Cmd + Shift + R

2. Test in an Incognito / Private Window:
   On Chrome: Press Ctrl + Shift + N, then go to rightcomfort.ca

3. Give it 30–60 seconds:
   The automated system takes a short moment to send the new files to internet servers worldwide.


HELPFUL THINGS TO KNOW
----------------------
* You NEVER need to press any separate "Publish" button — saving on GitHub does it automatically.
* Nobody else on the internet can edit your website code unless you log them in.
* If you ever make a mistake while editing, GitHub keeps a history of all your old saved versions so you can go back anytime.
